WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.498
In 1978, mainland China began reform and opening up.

00:00:03.498 --> 00:00:07.004
Rural areas changed first, and farmers had new methods.

00:00:07.004 --> 00:00:10.350
A new era was slowly unfolding.

00:00:10.461 --> 00:00:14.899
Land was divided among households, raising motivation.

00:00:14.899 --> 00:00:18.653
Harvests in the fields got better year by year.

00:00:18.653 --> 00:00:21.428
Surplus grain could be taken to market to sell.

00:00:21.428 --> 00:00:25.127
Township enterprises slowly appeared, and factories grew in number.

00:00:25.187 --> 00:00:29.453
Markets became lively again, with goods growing ever richer.

00:00:29.453 --> 00:00:32.753
Coastal regions opened to the outside, and cities grew rapidly.

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:36.361
Shenzhen turned from a small fishing village into a big city.

00:00:36.361 --> 00:00:39.633
High-rises went up one after another, and roads grew wider.

00:00:39.633 --> 00:00:42.126
International trade became more and more frequent.

00:00:42.126 --> 00:00:45.788
Chinese goods began reaching world markets.

00:00:45.883 --> 00:00:49.050
Foreign businesspeople also came to China to invest.

00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:53.667
Reform and opening up brought enormous changes.

00:00:53.667 --> 00:00:56.640
People's lives also improved step by step.
